@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-rounding-order-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-rounding-order-5746`
IMPORT `ito-120b-d-rounding-power`

-- Tests for s 120B(d), the join between the Ordinance and the Rounding Order.
-- Expected values were worked by hand from the Order's rule before they were run.
-- The second group is a CONSISTENCY check, not law: each ceiling that s 121 prints (the
-- consolidation's current figures) is a whole multiple of 120 and so is a fixed point of Order s 1;
-- a figure that was not would show the printed ceiling and the Order disagreeing.
--   301,200 = 120 x 2,510 ; 560,280 = 120 x 4,669 ; 84,120 = 120 x 701 ; 120,720 = 120 x 1,006 ;
--   228,000 = 120 x 1,900.
-- The third group is the same check on the figures the notes after s 125D print for 2024-2027
-- (editorial notes, not law): 69,840 = 120 x 582 ; 10,920 = 120 x 91 ; 15,000 = 120 x 125 ;
-- 18,360 = 120 x 153. The Order has no rule for s 125D (fork R1), so they are a fixed point of the
-- step-120 rule only by practice, which the Order text does not state.

§ `Tests of s 120B(d)`

§§ `The join`
-- A hypothetical adjusted income ceiling 301_259.7: 301,200 + 59.7, below 60 -> 301,200.
-- The same as a credit point (step 12): 301_259.7 = 12 x 25,104 + 11.7 (301,248 + 11.7), 11.7 >= 6 -> 301,260.
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 301_259.7 `, of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 301_259.7 `, of the kind` `the amount of a credit point` EQUALS 301_260
-- A recognised donation amount: no rule in the Order, declined by default; kept as adjusted at the other reading.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 301_259.7 `, of the kind` `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 301_259.7 `, of the kind` `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)` `, reading an amount the Order has no rule for as` `such an amount stays as adjusted` EQUALS 301_259.7

§§ `The ceilings that section 121 prints are whole multiples of 120 (consistency, not law)`
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 301_200 `, of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 560_280 `, of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 560_280
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 84_120 `, of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 84_120
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 120_720 `, of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 120_720
#ASSERT `s 120B(d) — the amount after rounding` 228_000 `, of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 228_000

§§ `The figures the notes after section 125D print (editorial, not law)`
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 69_840 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 69_840
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 10_920 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 10_920
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 15_000 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 15_000
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 18_360 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 18_360
